I like the idea of the schema being more accurate (and the free port range validation), so I've pushed another commit. Thanks for the suggestions!

> I'm not 100% sure but I think that could expose an edge-case where a configuration has a connection block that has an invalid port and no provisioner blocks making use of it, which would previously have passed because it's the provisioner responsible for the validation

Good news! This does not break, because we only decode the `connection` block when iterating over the provisioners. The following config validates and applies normally with the commits on this branch:

```hcl
resource "null_resource" "foo" {
  connection {
    port = "boop"
  }
}
```
